# Build context for Dockerfile. vendor/ (toolkit submodule) is REQUIRED — do not ignore it.
# build/ and .next/ are regenerated inside the image (pnpm build:plugin && pnpm build).
# Both forms: a bare `node_modules` matches only the top-level entry, so the workspace member's
# own node_modules (packages/core/node_modules, full of host-specific pnpm symlinks) needs the
# glob or it would ride into the build context and shadow the image's install.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
build
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.git
.github
.claude
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
# Secrets / runtime data never enter the image (Next would otherwise copy .env into .next/standalone).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
data/runtime
# Phase-0 throwaway spike: never part of the server image.
spikes
apps
# Except the one plain module the demo corridor shares with sample mode (fixtures/demo/generate.ts imports it, and
# `next build` type-checks fixtures/** through the root tsconfig). It has no Capacitor or DOM imports.
!apps/ios/src/sample/shared.ts
# The UI/UX v1 browser harness (test-only). It imports the iOS fixture host under apps/, which is not
# in the image, and `next build` type-checks the root tsconfig's e2e/** and scripts/**: without these
# lines the image build fails with "Cannot find module '../../apps/ios/fixture-host/...'".
e2e/uiux
scripts/uiux-web
playwright.uiux.config.ts
sites
coverage
.vitest-cache
**/.DS_Store
